SUMMARY:Arthur Miller Lecture on Science and Ethics
LOCATION:MIT\, 292 Main St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:The Program in Science\, Technology\, and Society invites you t
 o the annual Arthur Miller Lecture in Science and Ethics on Monday\, Octob
 er 26th from 4:00-5:30 pm in the MIT Welcome Center\, for a panel lecture 
 on the use of chatbots in children's toys. The panel features Professor Mi
 mi Ito\, Director of the Connected Learning Lab\, Professor Sherry Turkle\
 , founding director of the MIT Initiative on Technology and Self\, and Mik
 e Rizkalla\, CEO & Founder of Snorble\, a visionary leader in AI\, consume
 r robotics\, humanoid robotics\, and children's technology.\nhttps://calen
 dar.mit.edu/event/arthur-miller-lecture-on-science-and-ethics-chatbots-in-
 childrens-toys-a-natural-progression-or-an-existential-crisis\nFrom Pushpi
 n Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/arthur-miller-lecture-on-science-and-eth
 ics-chatbots-in-childrens-toys-a-natural-progression-or-an-existential-cri
 sis
