UID:23257f2b827adf9c5b5baed37248b05a99d8926a@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20260926T213057Z
DTSTART:20261026T203000Z
DTEND:20261026T223000Z
SUMMARY:Innovation on Steroids:  What are We Learning from the Ukraine War?
LOCATION:MIT\, 33 MASSACHUSETTS AVE\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:Erik Lin Greenberg\, associate professor of political science\;
  co-director\, Wargaming Lab\, MIT Security Studies Program Erik Lin Green
 berg's research examines how emerging military technology affects conflict
  dynamics and the regulation and use of force. His book\, The Remote Revol
 ution: Drones and Modern Statecraft (Cornell University Press)\, explores 
 how remote warfighting technologies are reshaping international politics. 
 In other ongoing projects\, he explores how technology and public opinion 
 influence international politics and decisions on the use of force. He is 
 also interested in the international politics of food and the use of warga
 ming as a tool of scholarly inquiry. Before entering academia\, he was an 
 active duty officer in the United States Air Force and completed assignmen
 ts in operational units\, Headquarters Air Force\, and the Joint Staff. He
  currently commands a squadron in the Air Force Reserve.\nhttps://calendar
 .mit.edu/event/focus-on-eurasia-innovation-on-steroids-what-are-we-learnin
 g-from-the-ukraine-war\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/focus-on-eurasia-innovation-on-steroids-
 what-are-we-learning-from-the-ukraine-war
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
